  "title": "Honor Christ's body in the poor",
  "source": "Homily 50 on Matthew, 4 (NPNF 1/10)",
  "text": "Would you do honor to Christ's body? Neglect Him not when naked. Do not, while here you honor Him with silken garments, neglect Him perishing without, of cold and nakedness. For He that said, This is my body, the same said, You saw me an hungered, and fed me not. Let us learn therefore to honor Christ as He Himself desires. For God has no need at all of golden vessels, but of golden souls.",
